-- Agencies for CSC TIMS — the employer list behind the profile form's picker.
--
-- Generated from jportal_agencies.csv. The JSON counterpart
-- (database/data/agencies.json) is the one the application seeds from; this
-- file exists for loading straight into a database that already exists, or for
-- a DBA who would rather read SQL than JSON. Keep the two in step.
--
-- Field offices are looked up by CODE, never by a literal id. Ids are assigned
-- by whichever migration ran first on a given machine, so a dump carrying them
-- would file every agency under the wrong office on any other installation.
-- An office code this deployment does not have leaves the agency's office NULL,
-- which the profile form handles by asking the participant instead.
--
-- Safe to re-run: ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE corrects an existing row in place.
-- Deliberately never DELETEs — profiles point at these rows. Retire an agency
-- by setting is_active = 0, which keeps it on the profiles that already name it
-- while removing it from the picker.
--
-- `code` is the source list's own id and is what identifies a row across
-- re-runs. It is here so that correcting a NAME is an update rather than a
-- second agency — matching on name cannot tell a rename from a new employer,
-- and forks the row, stranding every profile already linked on the old one.
--
-- NOTE, unlike the seeder: this file cannot carry a corrected name or sector
-- out to the profiles already linked to the row. That propagation lives in the
-- `saved` hook on App\Models\Agency, which only Eloquent fires. After loading
-- this file over rows that already have participants attached, run
-- `php artisan db:seed --class=AgencySeeder` as well, or the reference and the
-- profiles will disagree.

START TRANSACTION;

ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE
    `name` = VALUES(`name`),
    `sector` = VALUES(`sector`),
    `field_office_id` = VALUES(`field_office_id`),
    `updated_at` = NOW();

COMMIT;
